#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:2
msgid "Ad blocking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:4
msgid ""
"Ad blockers fulfill a legitimate need to mitigate the significant "
"downsides of advertising from tracking across the internet, security "
"implications of third-party code, and impacting the UX and performance of"
" sites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:10
msgid ""
"At Read the Docs, we specifically didn't want those things. That's why we"
" built the our :doc:`Ethical Ad initiative <ethical-advertising>` with "
"only relevant, unobtrusive ads that respect your privacy and don't do "
"creepy behavioral targeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:15
msgid ""
"Advertising is the single largest source of funding for Read the Docs. To"
" keep our operations sustainable, we ask that you either :ref:`allow our "
"EthicalAds <advertising/ad-blocking:Allowing EthicalAds>` or :ref:`go ad-"
"free <advertising/ad-blocking:Going ad-free>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:22
msgid "Allowing EthicalAds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:24
msgid ""
"If you use AdBlock or AdBlockPlus and you allow `acceptable ads`_ or "
"`privacy-friendly acceptable ads`_ then you're all set. Advertising on "
"Read the Docs complies with both of these programs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:29
msgid ""
"If you prefer not to allow acceptable ads but would consider allowing "
"`ads that benefit open source`_, please consider subscribing to either "
"the wider **Open Source Ads list** or simply the **Read the Docs Ads "
"list**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:34
msgid "`Setup for AdBlock`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:35
msgid "`Setup for AdBlockPlus`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:36
msgid "`Setup for uBlock Origin`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:40
msgid ""
"Because of the way Read the Docs is structured where docs are hosted on "
"many different domains, adding a normal ad block exception will only "
"allow that single domain not Read the Docs as a whole."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:53
msgid "Going ad-free"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:55
msgid ""
"`Gold members <https://app.readthedocs.org/accounts/gold/>`_ may "
"completely remove advertising for all visitors to their projects. Thank "
"you for supporting Read the Docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:61
msgid ""
"Previously, Gold members or `Supporters "
"<https://app.readthedocs.org/sustainability/#donations>`_ were provided "
"an ad-free reading experience across all projects on Read the Docs while "
"logged-in. However, the cross-site cookies needed to make that work are "
"no longer supported by major browsers outside of Chrome, and this feature"
" has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:69
msgid "Statistics and data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:71
msgid ""
"It can be really hard to find good data on ad blocking. In the spirit of "
"transparency, here is the data we have on ad blocking at Read the Docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:75
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`32% of Read the Docs users use an ad blocker "
"<https://blog.readthedocs.com/ads-and-adblocking/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:76
msgid ""
"Of those, `a little over 50% allow acceptable ads "
"<https://blog.readthedocs.com/ad-blocker-update/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:77
msgid ""
"Read the Docs users running ad blockers click on ads at about the same "
"rate as those not running an ad blocker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:79
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Comparing with our server logs, roughly 28% of our hits did not register "
"a Google Analytics (GA) pageview due to an ad blocker, privacy plugin, "
"disabling JavaScript, or another reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/advertising/ad-blocking.rst:82
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Of users who do not block GA, about 6% opt out of analytics on Read the "
"Docs by enabling :ref:`Do Not Track <privacy-policy:Do Not Track>`."
msgstr ""

